stx_btree is a derivative work: its data structures, node layouts,
algorithms, concurrency protocol and many of their comments are translated
from bbtree's Rust source at commit 8adae97a0ed97e5c98fa2790312eb0aec9719846
and from its design documents (design/*.md, decisions D1-D60). Every file
was rewritten in C++20; the changes made in translation, and what was not
translated, are listed in PROVENANCE.md and docs/DESIGN.md.

Decision numbers (Dnn) and document names cited in the source refer to
bbtree's design/03-decisions.md and design/*.md at that commit.

The optimal search tree components (include/stx_btree/search_weights.hpp,
optimal_tree.hpp, detail/monge_product.hpp) implement the construction of
"Core-Sparse Monge Construction for Full Optimal Binary Search Trees" by
OpenAI Codex Sydney (problem selection and sponsorship: Joshuah Rainstar),
https://github.com/falseywinchnet/papers_please (obst/), commit
eef656fae6e6bf65fd19b5f74abc6081ad6e67f7. detail/monge_product.hpp and the
layer construction in optimal_tree.hpp are a rewrite of its prototype
obst/code/compact_obst.cpp, which is distributed under this license:

